+## Correction (appended, round 76 — R1 of the round-75 verifier spot-check)
+
+**Superseded text — M75-1 (`corpus/lessons/round-75.md:11`) and the Gate reject candidate (`:5`).** The mistake row said "`considerthese/2026-10-26.md:17` says description is 1,021/1,024 characters; current committed SKILL frontmatter (master 65a5c7a, lines 3–18) is substantially shorter" and closed on "This lesson-only repair is not claimed as a guard until a failing fixture demonstrates it." The Gate said "Candidate reject: any claim that the 1021-character description size reported in `considerthese/2026-10-26.md` remains current; current frontmatter is materially shorter." Both premises are false. The description renders **1,022 characters** — YAML folded scalar `>` under `description: >` at line 3, block content lines 4–18, closing `---` at line 19 — and 1,021 after the clip newline is stripped; the first sentence is 151 characters. `considerthese/2026-10-26.md:17`'s "still 1,021 of 1,024 chars" and "about 150 chars" are the current values at the r75 tip, not historical ones: the reject candidate is withdrawn and M75-1's `stale-premise` classification is withdrawn.
+
+The superseded row, verbatim (indented so it does not re-enter the `## Mistakes` table):
+
+    | stale-premise | `considerthese/2026-10-26.md:17` says description is 1,021/1,024 characters; current committed SKILL frontmatter (master 65a5c7a, lines 3–18) is substantially shorter; direct `awk 'NR>=3&&NR<=8{print NR ":" length($0) ":" $0}'` yields 14,76,78,73,79,72 for frontmatter lines 3–8. | Q67 (read proposal against actual file contract) does not catch stale values; corpus Q54/Q60 require reproducible counts and revision-addressed evidence, but no current criterion catches a proposal's imported observation | Freeze each proposed target from the current committed bytes and rerun its counter before plan freeze; classify historical proposal numbers as historical, not as round baseline. This lesson-only repair is not claimed as a guard until a failing fixture demonstrates it. |
+
+**Why the row's numbers reproduced and the conclusion still failed.** The six lengths are correct as raw line lengths, but the window covers 6 of the block's 16 source lines (the `description: >` marker on line 3 plus content lines 4–18), summing to 392 — and a raw line sum is not the scalar's value in two ways: `length($0)` counts the two-space YAML indent on every content line and the 14-character marker line, and folding replaces each line break with one space. Over the whole content block: 1,037 raw characters (lines 4–18) − 30 indentation + 14 join spaces = 1,021 folded, and `yaml.safe_load` keeps the clip newline → **1,022**.
+
+Slice, stated so the number is reproducible: the frontmatter slice must keep the block's trailing newline (`sys.stdin.read().split('---')[1]` does; slicing at the closing `\n---` drops it and reads 1,021). The convention is the frozen one: `plans/round-76-addendum-1.md` (committed `7eed80e9`) fixes clip-preserving = 1,022 and requires every receipt that prints the number to print both variants and name the convention.
+
+Measured from committed bytes at `b7f13f4b39cbd43076a85568adca763a6f674e7a` (identical description at `65a5c7a663249e0522cc49e4a148424200d9ddfe`, `ac9f29510d3914a6edb97c8dbdb3445cab9141de`, `4de12b61f75c73e3675ef0e422cc2be0f7da8960`):
