+- `git show b7f13f4:SKILL.md | awk 'NR>=4&&NR<=18{s+=length($0)} END{print s}'` → `1037`, exit 0; `awk 'NR>=3&&NR<=8{printf "%d:%d ",NR,length($0)}'` → `3:14 4:76 5:78 6:73 7:79 8:72` (sum 392), exit 0.
+- First sentence: `git show b7f13f4:SKILL.md | python3 -c "import sys,yaml;d=yaml.safe_load(sys.stdin.read().split('---')[1])['description'].strip();print(len(d.split('. ')[0]+'.'))"` → `151`, exit 0.
+
+**Re-derivation owed by R1.** The same premise was written into `plans/round-75.md:15` ("current description frontmatter lines 4–8 lengths are 76,78,73,79,72 (the stale 1,021-char assertion in `considerthese/2026-10-26.md` is not the current base)"). No round-75 claim consumed it — round 75's C1 is the equality-threshold claim on `SKILL.md:193` — so this correction withdraws the plan's base note and the Gate reject; nothing else in round 75 rests on the number. The number is restated by the frozen counter `python3 -B verifiers/check_r75_routed_repairs.py --rev <rev>`; its receipt `.ufo/waves/round-76/receipts/r1-folded-render.txt` is required by the addendum to recompute the render from the measured revision's `SKILL.md`, print both variants (clip 1,022 / stripped 1,021) and name the convention.
